# Mediawiki get-code

Can be used to retrieve code easily from Gerrit.

You can persist some configurable settings in the config.

```sh
mw config get gerrit.username
mw config set gerrit.username foo
```

New clones receive Wikimedia Gerrit's official `commit-msg` hook, including when
cloning from a GitHub mirror before switching the remote to Gerrit. This adds
Change-Id trailers when you commit. Existing hooks and any configured
`core.hooksPath` are preserved. Use `--no-commit-hook` to skip the download;
`--dry-run` never downloads or installs a hook. A hook download failure is reported
as a warning after the clone, with a link to Gerrit's manual setup instructions.


Use `--jobs 4` (or `-j 4`) to clone up to four independent skins/extensions at a
time. Core is always cloned first. The default is one job, preserving serial
interactive Git authentication; use an SSH agent or cached HTTPS credentials
for parallel clones. Duplicate requested repositories are cloned once. Errors
are returned to the caller and reported in request order.
